# Title: Suspicious File Created Via OneNote Application
# ID: fcc6d700-68d9-4241-9a1a-06874d621b06
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2023-02-09
# Tags: attack.stealth
# Description: Detects suspicious files created via the OneNote application. This could indicate a potential malicious ".one"/".onepkg" file was executed as seen being used in malware activity in the wild
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((process.executable:*\\onenote.exe OR process.executable:*\\onenotem.exe OR process.executable:*\\onenoteim.exe) AND file.path:*\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\OneNote\\* AND (file.path:*.bat OR file.path:*.chm OR file.path:*.cmd OR file.path:*.dll OR file.path:*.exe OR file.path:*.hta OR file.path:*.htm OR file.path:*.html OR file.path:*.js OR file.path:*.lnk OR file.path:*.ps1 OR file.path:*.vbe OR file.path:*.vbs OR file.path:*.wsf))
